(GRM-15: print_stmt's three forms - plain "Print" expr with a "but if"
 tail (note: THIS "but if" has no "then" and no comma before the
 branch's own "print", unlike if_stmt's "but if...then," - GRM-12 - two
 different productions sharing the words "but if"), "Print each name from
 expr (treating)? " with a "but if" tail, and "Print <func> of each name
 from expr" (the function-return-per-item form). A firing "but if" arm
 REPLACES the base Print for that iteration, it does not print
 alongside it (see EXA-05, which is this exact plain form at scale).
 Cross-ref FMT (input-output.md, the plain form) and LST2/BAS2
 (collections-b.md, basics-expansion.md, the each/treating forms), which
 map this production's full claim set.
